# File: specs/bug-fix-start-issue-shortlist-starvation/feature.gherkin
# Issue: #175

Feature: Start-issue shortlist backfill
  As a developer selecting ready work
  I want discovery to look beyond a starved initial candidate window
  So that completed or blocked work does not hide actionable issues

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Discovery expands after the initial window starves
    Given the first ten open issues contain fewer than four selectable candidates
    And later open issues in the same scope are selectable
    When bare start-issue discovery runs
    Then the fetch limit expands in ten-issue increments
    And the ordered candidate prefix is reevaluated from fresh evidence
    And expansion stops at four choices, scope exhaustion, or 100 inspected issues

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: All-Done Project work is excluded automatically
    Given an open issue has one or more readable Project statuses
    And every readable status equals Done case-insensitively
    When automatic discovery builds its shortlist
    Then the issue is excluded separately from dependency-blocked issues
    And missing, unreadable, or mixed statuses do not prove completion

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit selection can reopen Done work
    Given the user supplies an issue number explicitly or through manual entry
    And every readable Project status is Done
    When the issue confirmation is presented
    Then the issue remains selectable
    And the user is warned that starting it will move completed Project work to In Progress

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Expanded discovery preserves readiness safety
    Given an expanded candidate prefix contains coordination and execution relationships
    When discovery evaluates issues needed to fill the shortlist
    Then complete pagination and hydration are required
    And relationship and deliverable failures remain fail-closed
    And topological ordering uses only verified execution dependencies
    And unrelated trailing records cannot abort or reorder an already-complete shortlist

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: PathCast-shaped backfill performs no mutation
    Given ten initial candidates are blocked or Done
    And four later candidates are ready
    When disposable bare discovery runs
    Then the four later candidates are reported
    And the Done candidate is omitted
    And no branch, issue, Project, or repository mutation occurs
